  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The wall stood straight from top to bottom and floated in mid air like a giant mirror, with Book Mountain inside that mirror. After it broke, it turned into numerous grey-white stone slabs.",
      "chapters": [
        495
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "While inspecting grey-white stone slabs taken from Chai tribe resources in Ge tribe camp, Fang Yuan recalls that Carefree Wisdom Heart came to the Qian Kun Crystal Wall to save Wisdom Gu. The wall stood straight from top to bottom and floated in mid air like a giant mirror, with Book Mountain inside that mirror. On the book mountain an ink waterfall landed on the rocks to form a literature spring, and black splashes formed into words, the origin of the hundred clan writing system. After the wall broke, it turned into numerous grey-white stone slabs. Legends say that gathering all of the slabs could piece back the wall and let a Gu Master enter book mountain again. Generations of Gu Masters, Gu Immortals, and even Immortal and Demon Venerables collected these slabs, and large numbers of counterfeits appeared. The most authoritative appraiser named in that stretch is treasure yellow heaven’s owner, Daoist Countless Treasures, who still only reached seventy to eighty percent accuracy on fakes. Even Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable purposely made convincing fakes. Fang Yuan does not plan to collect every slab to restore book mountain, since even a rank nine Gu Venerable did not succeed.",
      "chapters": [
        495
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grey-white-stone-slabs",
